CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^\[main\.assertion\.\d+\] line \d+ assertion \*g\.q == 0: FAILURE$
--
--
Checks that a read through a pointer stored in a field of a global struct,
which the alias analysis does not track, may read any variable whose address is
taken: `t` holds the previous iteration's value when it is read through
`g.q`, so it is not a loop local.
